    "why": "The word 'fully' is doing all the work in this row, and this is the case that separates the two readings of it. p-ali's call starts at eight on the 5th and ends at eight on the 6th, so no duty row is dated the 6th and the person was in the hospital for a third of it — 'no on-duty minute' makes the 6th occupied and 'no duty row dated D' makes it free, which is the difference between a rule that protects rest and one that reports it was protected. p-noor holds a duty on the same date under a slot that ends the same evening, so their 6th really is free: same anchor date, opposite answer, and the only thing between them is the occupied-interval reading. The third person is here because a PLANT STAYED GREEN: deleting CG-01's scope from this type changed nothing anywhere in the corpus, since no case of it set one — the same defect P2-1's review found thirteen times, reappearing on all four remaining window types at once. p-zaid rotates on NICU and would be flagged on their own figures; the scope naming PICU is the only thing between them and a violation.",
